# The loop contact set for the d26_s1 close-up. Sets no camera, so it can be
# run on a view already positioned by hand.
#
# Written to be re-runnable. Creating a distance that already exists is an
# error in ChimeraX, and an error aborts the rest of a .cxc, which is why an
# earlier version drew one dashed line and then silently stopped before the
# labels. Everything is therefore torn down first and rebuilt.
#
# Shown, both with their distance:
#   Asp42 OD1 - Arg8  NH1   3.72 A   carboxylate to guanidinium, a salt bridge
# Arg33 is no longer drawn at all. Its closest approach to Asp42 is OD2 to CB
# at 3.19 A, a carbon in the side-chain stem; the nearest charged nitrogen is
# NE at 4.89 A, with the rest of the guanidinium 5.6 to 7.7 A away. Showing a
# labelled arginine beside a labelled aspartate invites the reader to assume a
# salt bridge that is not there, and dropping the dashed line without dropping
# the residue would make that worse, not better.
#
# Val32 CG1 at 4.47 A is dropped: uncharged, and the longest of the three.

~distance
label delete
hide #2 atoms

# `color ... & sidechain` also repaints the residue's ribbon, so residues that
# were highlighted in an earlier run keep their grey cartoon after their atoms
# are hidden. Val32 is the case in point. Resetting the chain colours first
# undoes any of that.
color #2 cornflower blue
color #2/B light green
color #2/A:33-51 red
color #2/A:79-84 purple
color #2/A:22,26,31 goldenrod

show #2/A:42 #2/B:8 atoms
style #2/A:42 #2/B:8 stick
size #2/A:42 #2/B:8 stickRadius 0.13
# Grey carbons with element-coloured tips, matching the side-chain treatment in
# the d39 figure so the two structure figures read as one set. Restricted to
# atoms, so the ribbons keep their chain colour. The panel is now a close-up
# framed on the contact, so there is no longer any risk of the side chains
# being read as belonging to the wrong chain.
color #2/A:42 & sidechain dark slate gray atoms
color #2/B:8 & sidechain dark slate gray atoms
color #2/A:42 & sidechain byhetero atoms
color #2/B:8 & sidechain byhetero atoms

distance #2/A:42@OD1 #2/B:8@NH1
distance style color black dashes 8 radius 0.05 decimalPlaces 2

label #2/A:42 text "Asp42" height 1.1 color black offset -3.4,-2.2,0
label #2/B:8 text "Arg8" height 1.1 color black offset 2.2,0.3,0
